 that have them.","body":["For a vector, the missing elements go; for a matrix, the rows with any missing element (the columns with `dim` 2), or only those with at least `'MinNumMissing'`; for a table, the rows with a missing value in its variables."],"syntax":[["R = rmmissing(A)","Without them."],["R = rmmissing(A, dim)","Columns instead (dim 2)."],["[R, TF] = rmmissing(..., 'MinNumMissing', n)","Rows with at least n missing, and which were removed."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"A vector and a matrix","intro":"","code":"rmmissing([1 NaN 3 NaN 5])\nA = [1 2; NaN 4; 5 NaN; 7 8];\n[R, TF] = rmmissing(A)","after":"","output":"ans =\n\n     1     3     5\n\nR =\n\n     1     2\n     7     8\n\nTF =\n\n  4×1 logical array\n\n   0\n   1\n   1\n   0","figures":[]}],"notes":[],"see":["fillmissing","ismissing"]},{"names":["standardizeMissing"],"summary":"Values that stand for \"missing\" made the standard missing value.","body":["Data often mark gaps with a code such as -99 or `'N/A'`; `standardizeMissing` makes them NaN (or empty text, NaT or undefined) so that the functions that know missing values treat them as such."],"syntax":[["B = standardizeMissing(A, indicators)","The indicators made missing."],["B = standardizeMissing(T, indicators, 'DataVariables', vars)","In a table's variables."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"A code for no reading","intro":"","code":"y = [12.1 -99 13.4 -99 12.8];\nB = standardizeMissing(y, -99)\nmean(B, 'omitnan')","after":"","output":"B =\n\n   12.1000       NaN   13.4000       NaN   12.8000\n\nans =\n\n   12.7667","figures":[]}],"notes":[],"see":["fillmissing","ismissing"]},{"names":["isoutlier"],"summary":"Which values are outliers.","body":["By default a value more than 3 scaled median absolute deviations from the median, which outliers themselves hardly move; `'mean'` uses 3 standard deviations, `'quartiles'` 1.5 interquartile ranges beyond the quartiles, `'grubbs'` and `'gesd'` statistical tests, and `'movmedian'` and `'movmean'` a moving window for data that drift. `'ThresholdFactor'` changes the 3; the other outputs give the thresholds and the centre."],"syntax":[["TF = isoutlier(A)","By scaled median absolute deviation."],["TF = isoutlier(A, method)","By another method."],["TF = isoutlier(A, 'movmedian', window)","Within a moving window."],["[TF, L, U, C] = isoutlier(..., 'ThresholdFactor', t)","With the thresholds and centre."]],"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"examples":[{"title":"Two outliers found","intro":"","code":"x = [2.1 2.3 1.9 2.2 9.5 2.0 2.4 -4 2.1];\n[TF, L, U, C] = isoutlier(x)\nfind(TF)","after":"","output":"TF =\n\n  1×9 logical array\n\n   0   0   0   0   1   0   0   1   0\n\nL =\n\n    1.2104\n\nU =\n\n    2.9896\n\nC =\n\n    2.1000\n\nans =\n\n     5     8","figures":[]},{"title":"In drifting data, with a moving window","intro":"","code":"rng default\nt = (1:100)';\ny = t/10 + 0.3*randn(100, 1);\ny([30 70]) = y([30 70]) + 4;\ntf = isoutlier(y, 'movmedian', 15);\nplot(t, y, '.', t(tf), y(tf), 'ro'), legend('data', 'outliers', 'Location', 'northwest')","after":"","output":"","figures":[{"id":1,"type":"figure","number":1,"name":"","numberTitle":true,"width":560.0,"height":420.0,"color":[0.94,0.94,0.94],"visible":true,"version":6,"windowStyle":"normal","axes":[{"id":2,"type":"axes","kind":"cartesian","geo":false,"position":[0.13,0.11,0.775,0.815],"xlim":[0.0,100.0],"ylim":[-2.0,12.0],"zlim":[0.0,1.0],"xlimMode":"auto","ylimMode":"auto","zlimMode":"auto","clim":[0.0,1.0],"tight":{"X":false,"Y":false,"Z":false},"xscale":"linear","yscale":"linear","zscale":"linear","xdir":"normal","ydir":"normal","zdir":"normal","xgrid":false,"ygrid":false,"zgrid":false,"xminorgrid":false,"yminorgrid":false,"zminorgrid":false,"box":true,"color":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"xcolor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"ycolor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"zcolor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"gridColor":[0.15,0.15,0.15],"gridAlpha":0.15,"gridLineStyle":"-","fontSize":10.0,"lineWidth":0.5,"tickDir":"in","view":[0.0,90.0],"camTar